---
description: Never commit, push, or ask to do either unless the user explicitly requests it
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git: no auto commit / push

- Never run `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks for it in the current message.
- Never ask, offer, or suggest committing or pushing. Do not end replies with “veux-tu que je committe / pousse ?” or similar.
- If changes are ready locally, say so factually (files changed, what remains for the user). Do not solicit a commit/push decision.
- Preparing changes, staging suggestions, and showing a commit message draft is fine when asked — executing commit/push is not.
- Fixing CI or finishing a PR does not imply permission to commit or push.
